{
  "title": "Multiple Epiphyseal Dysplasia (MED)",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4095/multiple-epiphyseal-dysplasia-med",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Sep 25 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Multiple Epiphyseal Dysplasia is a congenital disorder caused most commonly by an autosomal mutation in cartilage oligomeric matrix protein on chromosome 19. Patients present with a form of dwarfism characterized by irregular, delayed ossification at multiple epiphyses.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made radiographically with presence of irregular, delayed ossification at multiple epiphyses.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually physical therapy and pain management. Surgical osteotomies and arthroplasty are indicated in patients with progressive deformity or degenerative joint disease.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Prevalence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approximately 1:10000",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "presents between age 5-14 years of age",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "caused by failure of formation of secondary ossification center (epiphysis)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "delay of epiphyseal endochondral ossification",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "lack of osseous support yields secondary articular cartilage deformity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "most commonly affects **proximal femur and proximal humerus**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Genetics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**autosomal dominant is most common**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**mutation in COMP (cartilage oligomeric matrix protein) gene on chromosome 19 (most common and most severe form)**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "mutations **type IX collagen**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "COL9A1, COL9A2, COL9A3",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "causing **type II collagen dysfunction** because of type IX collagen acts as a link protein for type II collagen",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "necessary for healthy articular cartilage",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "Mutation in **Matrillin 3**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "may also be autosomal recessive",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "mutation in SLC26A2 (diastrophic dysplasia **sulfate transporter** gene)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "presents with at least one finding at birth",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "clubfoot, cleft palate, clinodactyly",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "up to half of patients with clinical diagnosis of MED do not have the typical genetic mutations",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**short-limbed, disproportionate dwarfism**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "joint pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "waddling gait",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "joint deformities from joint incongruity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "hips are most common joint involved",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "valgus knee deformity common",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "early OA",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "joint contractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "short, stubby fingers and toes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "normal neurologic exam",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "normal intelligence",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "spine is normal",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "normal facies",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "general findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**demonstrate irregular, delayed ossification at multiple epiphyses**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4095/images/Xray%20-%20knee%20-%20col_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": "AP bilateral knee radiograph"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**may also demonstrate multiple osteochondritis dissecans lesions**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "hip",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may show bilateral proximal femoral epiphyseal defects",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4095/images/med%20radiographs.jpg",
                      "caption": "Patella can have a double layer appearance and hip involvement is usually bilateral"
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4095/images/Xray%20-%20pelvis%20-%20colorado_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "distinguished from Legg-Calve-Perthes disease by its **symmetric and bilateral presentation, early acetabular changes, and lack of metaphyseal cysts**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "when bilateral Legg-Calve-Perthes is suspected, perform skeletal survey of other joints to rule out MED",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "concurrent avascular necrosis of femoral head",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "acetabular dysplasia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "knee",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "valgus knee",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "flattened femoral condyles",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "double layer patella",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4095/images/med%20radiographs.jpg",
                      "caption": "Patella can have a double layer appearance and hip involvement is usually bilateral"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "hand",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may show **short, stunted metacarpals**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "hyperextensible fingers",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "foot",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**short metatarsals**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Spondyloepiphyseal dysplasia",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "distinct in that it also involves the spine",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "typically with a sharp curve",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "atlantoaxial instability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "cervical myelopathy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**mutation in type II collagen**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "NSAIDS and physical therapy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "early OA",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "childhood hip deformities such as acetabular dysplasia often resolve by skeletal maturity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "realigning osteotomy or hemiepiphysiodesis at the knee",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "progressive genu varum or valgum",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "total hip arthroplasty",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "severe arthritis may present by age 30",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
